# SnapSurf Intel Register Discipline

Compiler-internal NASM routines:
- Follow `compiler/inc/calling_conv.inc`.
- Save `rbx`, `r12`, `r13`, `r14`, and `r15` when a routine keeps state in them
  across nested calls.
- Treat `rax`, `rcx`, `rdx`, `rsi`, `rdi`, and `r8-r11` as scratch unless the
  local routine explicitly saves them.

Generated SnapSurf code:
- Function return value: `rax`.
- Integer argument registers in order: `rdi`, `rsi`, `rdx`, `rcx`, `r8`, `r9`.
- Parameters are spilled into stack slots on entry. The current emitter then
  reuses the existing local-load/store path instead of inventing a second
  parameter access path.
- User functions are rejected above six parameters until stack-passed arguments
  are implemented deliberately.

Review rule:
- Any assembly change that moves data through `mov`, `push`, `pop`, `call`, or
  `ret` must be reasoned at register/stack-slot level before it is called done.
